# Timesheet context

Source of truth for *who's who* and *which client each activity belongs to*. The skill reads it every
run and proposes additions (with a diff) when it learns something — merge those, don't duplicate. Keep
it tight: only confirmed facts. Delete sections you don't use. Hand-edit any time.

> **Keep this file lean.** It's loaded into context on every run, so terse facts beat prose. Use short
> bullets, drop unused sections, and don't let it bloat — fewer tokens here means a faster, cheaper run.

## Preferences

Override skill defaults. Omit any line to keep the default.

- **Timezone**: `Pacific/Auckland`  <!-- IANA; drives AW UTC→local -->
- **AFK break threshold**: `1050s` (17.5 min) — shorter folds into work
- **Lunch window**: `11:30`–`14:30` local
- **Work-hours render window**: `06:00`–`20:00` local
- **Default task (client work)**: `Gen - Development/Configuration`
- **Default task (internal/admin)**: `Meeting - Standup Meetings`
- **Display name in window titles**: `<YourFirstName>`  <!-- Edge titles end `… - <Profile> - <YourFirstName> - Microsoft Edge` -->

## AW buckets

Hostname suffix (cached after first discovery): `<YOUR-MACHINE-NAME>`. Buckets follow
`aw-watcher-{window,afk,web-firefox,web-chrome,vscode}_<HOST>`.

## Internal colleagues

Names that, in a Teams title, mean internal work (not a client):
- `<Full Name>` — `<role, optional>`

## Known external contacts

Externals you regularly chat with → auto-classify to a client:
- `<Full Name>` → `<client>`  <!-- Teams "(External unfamiliar)" flag is often stale -->

## Active client projects

One block per client. List every signal that identifies the client without asking.

### <Client Name>

- **Harvest client**: `<exact name in Harvest>`
- **Default project**: `<code>` `<name>`
- **Signals** (include the ones that apply):
  - Title/URL token: `<token>` or bracket tag `[<CODE>]`
  - Edge profile: `<ProfileName>`
  - Dynamics env: `<env>.crm6.dynamics.com`
  - ChatGPT project / Azure DevOps org / SharePoint subdomain: `<...>`
  - VS Code workspace `<name>` / repo path `<path>`
  - Teams team `<name>`
- **Typical work**: `<free text>`

### <Client Name 2>

…repeat.

## Shared signals (optional)

If clients share a codebase/meeting, note the split rule:
- `<Client A>` + `<Client B>` (both `<Parent>`): recurring `<Meeting>` → `<project>`; repo `<repo>` → pick by ticket.

## How I bill

- **Descriptions**: client-readable, 5–15 words, outcome-first. No file/tool/internal-app names (they
  go on invoices). Markdown audit file can be more granular than the Harvest `notes` field.
- **Bill by ticket/work item, not by window/app** — one ticket = one entry even across many apps.
- **Catalog existence ≠ today's target**; **codebase path ≠ billing target** — use work-item context.
- Examples (paste 3–5 of your own): `<outcome>` · `<outcome>` · `<outcome>`

## Exclude (never bill)

- Personal browsing (flights, social, news, weather, shopping, personal email)
- Pomodoro/timer pages; home admin (router, smart home, NAS)
- Harvest's own Timesheet tab → internal admin, not client work

## Inference notes

- Edge profile in title = strong client signal.
- Teams meeting names = reliable block boundaries.
- `data.app == "unknown"` / empty title ≈ locked screen — don't bill.
- Pure `claude.exe` next to timesheet-automation paths (`Claude/Scheduled/`, `Pictures/WorkScreenshots/`,
  `Timesheets/`) → internal admin; next to a client's app stack → that client.
